  "markdown": "Edgware Road, Paddington, London W2\n\n# Hilton London Metropole\n\nJet-black Muraspec wallcovering, and Vescom wallcovering on the wall panels of a large conference room, at the Hilton London Metropole in Paddington in 2019.\n\n![Large conference room at the Hilton London Metropole with Vescom-covered wall panels.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-05-800.webp)\n\n## At a glance\n\nClient, materials & project facts\n\n**Client**\n: Hilton London Metropole\n\n**Designer**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Main contractor**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Maker and paper**\n: Muraspec; Vescom\n\n**Area or rooms**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Scope**\n: Wallcoverings, including conference-room wall panels\n\n**Year**\n: 2019\n\nTwo jobs at the Hilton London Metropole in Paddington in the autumn of 2019: a jet-black embossed Muraspec wallcovering in September, and in November a Vescom wallcovering on the wall panels of one of the hotel’s large conference rooms.\n\n## At a glance\n\n- **Hotel:** Hilton London Metropole, Paddington\n- **When:** September to November 2019\n- **Scope:** wallcoverings, including the wall panels of a conference room\n- **Wallcoverings:** Muraspec (jet black), Vescom\n\n## Wall panels in a conference room\n\nPanelled walls in a conference room are covered panel by panel. Each panel is wrapped so the wallcovering runs the same way on every one, and the edges meet the neighbouring panels on a clean line, because the room is seen all at once from the doors.\n\n## Photographs on this page\n\nOur own photographs, first posted on our Instagram, [@mrwallcover](https://www.instagram.com/mrwallcover/), in September and November 2019: the conference room first, then the wallcoverings and the hotel. The work is recorded in our posts of 29 September 2019 ([B3AAo9sFAE_](https://www.instagram.com/p/B3AAo9sFAE_/)) and 27 November 2019 ([B5XtSRtFedQ](https://www.instagram.com/p/B5XtSRtFedQ/)).\n\n## Photographs\n\n![Conference room with balcony rail and wallcovered panels, Hilton London Metropole.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-07-800.webp)\n\n![Conference room with patterned carpet and wallcovered panels, Hilton London Metropole.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-06-800.webp)\n\n![Doors to the Monarch Suite conference room at the Hilton London Metropole.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-04-800.webp)\n\n![Close-up of a jet-black textured Muraspec wallcovering, Hilton London Metropole.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-01-800.webp)\n\n![Detail of a jet-black embossed Muraspec wallcovering, Hilton London Metropole.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-02-800.webp)\n\n![Exterior of the Hilton London Metropole, Edgware Road.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/metropole-03-800.webp)\n\nHow the commission ran\n\n## The same standards, on every commission.\n\nWhether the client is a hotel group, a designer or a household, the job runs the same way. These are the parts a photograph never shows.\n\n01\n\n### Survey and scope, room by room\n\nWe measure the wall that will actually be hung, allow for the repeat and the wastage, and write a scope of works room by room before anyone orders paper.\n\n02\n\n### Preparation decides the finish\n\nWalls are filled, made good and primed until they are true. If a wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\n03\n\n### Protection and containment\n\nFloors, furniture and finished joinery are protected as part of the hang. Work is contained and the place is left tidy each evening. In a home we are visitors; in a hotel we work around the house.\n\n04\n\n### Batch and shade control\n\nDeliveries are checked against the measure, and batches and shading are managed so that a corridor of rooms reads as one surface.\n\n05\n\n### Set out from the room's focal points\n\nPattern is set out from chimneypieces, doorcases and bed walls, so the design meets the cornice and the joinery with composure.\n\n06\n\n### One team, then the return visit\n\nThe people who start are the people who finish. Four to six weeks after completion we come back to look at every seam and edge, and the workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months.\n\n[See the finish up close: seams, internal corners, edges and joins from our own installations](https://www.mrwallcover.com/details/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 11 October 2026\n",
